{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3678","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3678","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3678\",\"parent_revision\":\"564dcd7c7bb40408f35f8a4672e7a2038c895bfb23ab3faaa11a38c88cefcc35\",\"root_revision\":\"564dcd7c7bb40408f35f8a4672e7a2038c895bfb23ab3faaa11a38c88cefcc35\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA Windows reader silently loses every rule and skill delivered this way. The failure gives no error: the file exists and parses, it just carries a path instead of content. An agent then works without the rule and nothing reports the gap.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCodex review flagged `.cursor/rules/json-no-pretty-print.mdc` on PR #3677 at P2. That PR converted one regular file into a symlink. The exposure covers all eight tracked symlinks, not only that one, and predates the PR for the other seven.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Codex suggested \\\"Keep the Cursor entry as a regular file, or materialize it through setup that is guaranteed to run before Cursor reads project rules.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\nBacklog reference (local cache, issue creation deferred because GraphQL is blocked in this session): `p2-tracked-symlinks-reach-windows-readers-as-plain-path-files-b`\\n\\n---\\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\\n</div>\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEvery harness reads the rule and skill content this repo delivers by symlink, on every supported platform.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEight paths are tracked with git mode 120000:\\n\\n- `.agent/skills/ccc`\\n- `.claude/skills/ccc`\\n- `.claude/skills/copy-editing`\\n- `.claude/skills/receiving-pr-reviews`\\n- `.claude/skills/workshop-question-framing`\\n- `.cursor/rules/json-no-pretty-print.mdc`\\n- `.pi/skills/ccc`\\n- `.pi/skills/copy-editing`\\n\\nOn a checkout where `core.symlinks` is false, Git writes each of these as a plain file whose entire content is the target path. A harness reading the path gets a one-line path string instead of the rule or skill body.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Clone the repo on a Windows workstation without Developer Mode or administrator rights, so Git sets `core.symlinks=false`.\\n2. Open Cursor before running any commit.\\n3. Read `.cursor/rules/json-no-pretty-print.mdc`. It contains `../../rules/json-no-pretty-print.mdc` and no rule text.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Timing Of The Existing Repair Path\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`scripts/repair_symlinks.py` is registered in `.pre-commit-config.yaml` with `stages: [pre-commit]`. It repairs these paths, but only when a commit runs. A fresh clone has no hooks installed until `prek install` runs, and a reader can open the repo before either happens. The script's own docstring records that symlink creation requires Windows Developer Mode or Administrator.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a51a1cdd3ac8259d8eb6c338ff148d6f6d9193c9937fd8b5d7495fbba12c4c56\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCEqAw\"}"}